<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2024_exam 26</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2024_EXAM 26 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 8/39<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 51 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:46:01.861Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT a valid use of decision coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Checking that all decisions have been exercised in a single program [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Checking that all decisions have been exercised in a business process</div><div class="opt ">c. Checking that all calls from one program module to another have been made correctly</div><div class="opt correct">d. Checking that at least 50% of decisions have been exercised by a test case suite [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.3.2 chọn D vì "least 50% of decisions" ko có yêu cầu này at least 50% là sai vì ko phải phần mềm nào cũng yêu cầu cái này</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">As part of the test strategy, entry and exit criteria will be defined for each test level. Which is NOT a valid reason for using entry and exit criteria?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The expectation is that development testing is not adequate. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Exit criteria are used to decide on when to stop testing.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Entry and exit criteria are a principal way for getting adequate resources. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Using entry and exit criteria will prevent software that is not or poorly tested from going to the next test level.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.3 Lý do nào KHÔNG hợp lệ để sử dụng tiêu chí vào và ra? Chọn C vì "adequate resources" là sai, entry và exit criteria để giúp trong tình huống thiếu thời gian và nguồn lực thì vẫn có thể test được những cái quan trọng nhất và đảm bảo mục tiêu quan trọng nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following phases in the fundamental test process is considered to deliver a document which can be used as a major input for test process improvement?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test planning and control [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test implementation &amp; execution</div><div class="opt ">c. Evaluating exit criteria and reporting</div><div class="opt correct">d. Test project closure [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.1 Giai đoạn nào sau đây trong quy trình kiểm thử cơ bản được coi là cung cấp một tài liệu có thể được sử dụng làm đầu vào chính để cải tiến quy trình kiểm thử? chọn D vì câu hỏi nhắc đến"test process improvement"</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">which of the following topics would you need to address in detail in the master test plan?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. An approach to regression testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. A list of boundary values for “advance amount”</div><div class="opt ">c. A description of dependencies between test cases</div><div class="opt ">d. A logical collection of test cases</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.1. chọn A vì có Approach, BCD là của test case</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">When comparing Static and Dynamic test techniques, which of the following statements is TRUE?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Static Testing finds failures, whilst Dynamic Testing only finds the cause of failures. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Static Testing techniques, such as reviews, can be undertaken before Dynamic Testing, making defects cheaper to remove. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Static Testing is based on the execution of code, whist Dynamic Testing relies on examination and analysis.</div><div class="opt ">d. Only Static Testing has the objective of identifying defects.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.1.2 Khi so sánh các kỹ thuật kiểm tra tĩnh và động, câu nào sau đây là ĐÚNG? Chọn B vì đúng như sách, loại A vì "Static Testing finds failures" failure là phải dynamic test mới tìm ra, loại C vì "Static Testing is based on the execution of code" loại D vì từ "Only"</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes checklist-based testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. An approach to testing whereby the testers dynamically design and execute tests based on their knowledge, exploration of the test item and the results of previous tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. An experience-based test technique whereby the experienced tester uses a high-level list of items to be noted, checked or remembered, or a set of rules or criteria against which a product has to be verified. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A procedure to derive and/or select test cases based on an analysis of the specification, either functional or non-functional, of a component or system without reference to its internal structure.</div><div class="opt ">d. A test design technique which ensures that test cases are checked for consistency and completeness against an organisation's list of formatting rules and best practices.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.4.3 Điều nào sau đây TỐT NHẤT mô tả thử nghiệm dựa trên checklist? Chọn B đúng "uses a high-level list of items to be noted, checked or remembered, or a set of rules or criteria- sử dụng danh sách ở mức cao các mục cần ghi chú, kiểm tra hoặc ghi nhớ hoặc một bộ quy tắc hoặc tiêu chí" loại A vì "dynamically" là của exploratory testing, loại C vì "analysis of the specification" của black box, loại D vì "ensures that test cases are checked for consistency and completeness against - cái này là kỹ thuật dùng checklist để review của chương 3 ko phải checklist để test</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a key difference between black box and white box test design techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Black box techniques use software code to derive test cases, white box techniques do not. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. White box techniques use functional design specifications to derive test cases, black box techniques do not.</div><div class="opt correct">c. White box techniques can measure the extent of code coverage, black box techniques can not. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. White box techniques derive test cases from models of the software, black box techniques do not.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.1 Điều nào sau đây là điểm khác biệt chính giữa kỹ thuật thiết kế kiểm thử hộp đen và hộp trắng? theo sách</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">A car insurance policy has 3 rates of insurance depending on the age of the driver. For drivers aged between 17 and 25 inclusive they are charged at rate A, drivers aged between 26 and 50 inclusive are charged at rate B and those drivers aged over 50 are charged at rate C. You are designing test cases, which of the following three ages would test all valid equivalence partitions and therefore test rate A, B and C?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 26, 45, 50. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 10, 21, 55.</div><div class="opt correct">c. 20, 35, 65. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 17, 25, 50.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">A student needs to score at least 50 points to pass. If they score at least 100 points they will achieve a merit and if they score at least 150 points they will achieve a distinction. Which two values are in the same partition?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 45 and 55. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 55 and 120.</div><div class="opt correct">c. 50 and 60. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 45 and 170.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would achieve the HIGHEST level of testing independence for a project's system test level?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Training developers to design good tests for the test team to execute. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Outsourcing test design and execution to a different company. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Having the company's independent test team design and execute the tests.</div><div class="opt ">d. Minimising contact between testers and developers during test design to avoid bias.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.3 Điều nào sau đây sẽ đạt được mức độ độc lập kiểm tra CAO NHẤT đối với cấp độ kiểm tra hệ thống của dự án? chọn D vì "Outsourcing" là cao nhất</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following apply to System Testing? a) May satisfy legal requirements. b) Can use system specifications as a test basis. c) Often the responsibility of business users. d) Main goal is to establish confidence. e) Should focus on the communication between systems.</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. a and c. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. b and d. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. a and b.</div><div class="opt ">d. c and e.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2. e là của integration test, a, c là rõ ràng nhất của Acceptance test, b là system test, còn d khá khiên cưỡng cho vào đây vì lẽ ra là của acceptance test, nhưng system test để test the whole system nên có thể chấp nhận đc mục tiêu về establish confidence</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">An issue has been found in a production system, where a code component fails to release memory after it has finished using it. Which of the following tools would have been the MOST effective at detecting this defect ?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Dynamic analysis tool. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test Execution tool.</div><div class="opt ">c. Configuration management tool.</div><div class="opt ">d. Coverage measurement tool.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 6.1 nó hỏi tool nào? mà trong đề bạn để ý "fails to release memory" nó mô tả về lỗi khi giải phóng bộ nhớ</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which option BEST describes how the level of risk is determined?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The likelihood of an adverse event happening multiplied by the cost of preventing it. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. The consequences of potential problem multiplied by the cost of possible legal action.</div><div class="opt correct">c. The impact of an adverse event multiplied by the likelihood of that event occurring. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The likelihood and the probability of a hazard occurring.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.2.1. Lựa chọn nào TỐT NHẤT mô tả cách xác định mức độ rủi ro? Bạn thấy risk level = likelihood x impact, nên chọn C vì có 2 nhân tố này, loại D vì probability = likelihood, loại A vì likelihood x the cost of preventing (2 cái này nhân với nhau là sai), loại B vì consequences x cost ( hậu quả nhân với chi phí)</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST describes how configuration management supports the test process?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. It enables the tester to reproduce the tested item through unique identification and version control [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. It enables the tester to systematically design test conditions, cases and data</div><div class="opt ">c. It enables incidents to be tracked from discovery and classification to correction and confirmation of the solution</div><div class="opt ">d. It helps the test manager to decide how best to integrate and coordinate the testing activities into the software life cycle.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.4 Điều nào sau đây TỐT NHẤT mô tả cách quản lý cấu hình hỗ trợ quá trình thử nghiệm? cứ theo định nghĩa ta chọn A vì có " unique identification and version control" loại B vì là mô tả của kỹ thuật thiết kế test của chương 4 mục 4.1.1, loại C vì nó đang mô tả đến defect management của 5.5, loại D vì là task của test manager ở mục 1.4.5</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">Which one of the following statements about techniques for estimating test effort is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The metrics-based technique finds the most similar former project and uses its original estimate for the current project. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. The expert-based approach is based on the experience of the owners of the testing tasks or by subject matter experts. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The metrics-based technique uses metrics supplied by the current test team based on their subjective feel for effort required.</div><div class="opt ">d. In an expert-based approach, the test lead with the most years in the role is chosen to produce the estimate.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.4 Câu nào sau đây về kỹ thuật ước lượng nỗ lực kiểm thử là đúng? Chọn B đúng mô tả đúng về expert-based, Loại A vì "uses its original estimate" sử dụng estimation ban đầu của các dự án tương tự để tham chiếu cho dự án hiện tại là sai, loại C vì "their subjective feel- cảm giác chủ quan" cái này ko thể của metric based, loại D vì "the most years" cho test lead nhiều năm kinh nghiệm nhất estimate là sai</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an approach that can be used for exploratory testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Time-boxed test sessions are created, during which a tester uses a test charter containing test objectives to guide the testing. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. A tester methodically executes tests from a list of possible failures, based on experience, defect and failure data.</div><div class="opt ">c. A tester analyses, designs and implements tests based on external rules and standards</div><div class="opt ">d. Tests are designed based on the guidance of stakeholders and experts outside the test team.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.4.2. Phương pháp nào sau đây có thể được sử dụng cho thử nghiệm thăm dò? Chọn A vì đúng với sách, loại B vì "list of possible failures" là của error guessing, loại C vì "based on external rules and standards" là của checklist, loại D vì "based on the guidance of stakeholders" test dựa vào hướng dẫn của các bên liên quan</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Given the following state transition diagram where SS is the start state: Which of the following answers describes a test case that only uses valid transitions to exercise all states, using the minimum number of transitions?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. SS-S3-SS-S1-S3-S2 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. SS-S3-S2-S1.</div><div class="opt ">c. SS-S1-S2-S3</div><div class="opt correct">d. SS-S1-S3-S2. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.4</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a key difference between black box and white box test design techniques?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Black box techniques use software code to derive test cases, white box techniques do not. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. White box techniques use functional design specifications to derive test cases, black box techniques do not.</div><div class="opt correct">c. White box techniques can measure the extent of code coverage, black box techniques can not. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. White box techniques derive test cases from models of the software, black box techniques do not</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.1.1 Điều nào sau đây là điểm khác biệt chính giữa black box and white box? chọn C như sách, A sai vì "Black box techniques use software code" B sai vì "White box techniques use functional design specifications" cái white box phải dùng detail technical design chứ ko phải tài liệu này, loại D vì "White box techniques derive test cases from models - dựa vào model là sai"</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following activities is appropriate to the test planning stage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Analyzing the test basis [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Assigning resources for the planned activities [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Designing the test environments</div><div class="opt ">d. Writing a test execution schedule</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.1 Hoạt động nào sau đây phù hợp với giai đoạn lập kế hoạch kiểm thử? chọn B như sách là của test planning, A là của test analysis, C là của test design, D là của test implementation</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">A booking system for a city bus service prices its fares according to the time of travel: Peak-time tariff starts at 06:00 and finishes at 10:00 am Off-peak tariff applied during all other times of services. The bus service does not operate between 23:00 and the start of the next day’s peak service. Note that all times mentioned are inclusive. When applying the equivalence partitioning test design technique, which of the following options shows test case inputs that each fall into a same equivalence partition?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 06:00, 10:00, 12:00 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 10:01, 13:00, 22:59 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 01:00, 08:00, 22:00</div><div class="opt ">d. 24:00, 10:00, 23:01</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.1</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">In the above State Table, which of the following represents an invalid transition?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Event C from S3 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Event E from S4</div><div class="opt ">c. Event B from S2</div><div class="opt correct">d. Event D from S4 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.4</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a characteristic of good testing in any life cycle model?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Analysis and design of tests begins as soon as development is completed. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Some, but not all, development activities have corresponding test activities</div><div class="opt correct">c. Each test level has test objectives specific to that level [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. All document reviews involve the development team.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.1.2 theo như sách nên chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would you expect to see in the master test plan?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A description of how the test cases are cross-referenced to requirements in the test management tool. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. A detailed identification of the resources that will carry out structural testing in the first iteration.</div><div class="opt correct">c. The test approach that will be applied at system integration testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. A list of the names of the testers who will carry out the performance testing for the final iteration.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.1 Bạn mong đợi điều nào sau đây trong kế hoạch kiểm tra tổng thể? chọn C vì "test approach"</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would be the TWO most appropriate examples of entry criteria documented in the system integration test plan?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. The percentage of decision coverage achieved during unit testing. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt selectedright">b. The availability of the latest version of the capture-replay tool (for testing the interface with the newly developed test management tool) [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. The sign-off of a performance test software release note (test item transmittal report) by both development and testing showing that system performance meets the specified acceptance criteria.</div><div class="opt ">d. The percentage of acceptance test procedures scheduled for execution.</div><div class="opt ">e. E. The percentage of requirements coverage achieved during system integration test</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 5.1.3 Điều nào sau đây sẽ là HAI ví dụ phù hợp nhất về tiêu chí đầu vào được ghi trong kế hoạch kiểm tra tích hợp hệ thống? chọn A vì là level trước (unit test) thỏa mãn tiêu chí kết thúc, Chọn B vì sự sẵn sàng của tài liệu</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a valid drawback of independent testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Developer and independent testing will overlap and waste resources. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Developers loose the sense of responsibility and independent testers may become a bottleneck. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Independent testers need extra education and always cost more</div><div class="opt ">d. Independent testers will become a bottleneck and introduce problems in incident management.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.5.3 Điều nào sau đây là nhược điểm hợp lý của thử nghiệm độc lập? chọn B đúng sách</div><h2>Cau hoi 26</h2><div class="qtext">When considering the roles of test leader and tester, which of the following tasks would NOT typically be performed by a tester?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Prepare and acquire the test data [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Set up and check the test environment</div><div class="opt correct">c. Write test summary reports [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Review tests developed by others</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.5 nhiệm vụ nào sau đây thường KHÔNG được tester thực hiện? chọn C vì của Leader</div><h2>Cau hoi 27</h2><div class="qtext">System requirement states that up to 100 users should be able to carry out a transaction, with responses returned within 5 seconds. What type of non-functional testing would you carry out to verify these requirements?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Stress testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Maintenance testing</div><div class="opt correct">c. Load testing [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Usability testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3. Bạn sẽ thực hiện loại thử nghiệm phi chức năng nào để xác minh các yêu cầu này? chọn đáp án là C. Cái này chưa đến mức stress test vì mới chỉ có 100 users thôi</div><h2>Cau hoi 28</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following would be a good test technique to use when you have only some days to test before release product?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Exploratory testing [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Structure based testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Specification based testing</div><div class="opt ">d. Use Case testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.4.2 Kỹ thuật thử nghiệm nào sau đây sẽ là kỹ thuật tốt để sử dụng khi bạn chỉ có vài ngày để thử nghiệm trước khi tung ra sản phẩm? chú ý vào "only some days" nên chọn A</div><h2>Cau hoi 29</h2><div class="qtext">The following Test Cases have been created for a simple web-based airline booking system. Test Case 1: Search for an item: Available Flights Test Case 2: View selected item in My Flights Test Case 3: Login to the system: Login is accepted Test Case 4: Select an available flight: item added to My Flights Test Case 5: Print confirmation receipt, then exit Test Case 6: In My Flights, confirm details and book flight Which of the following is the correct logical order for the test cases?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 6, 3, 1, 4, 2, 5 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 3, 4, 1, 2, 5, 6</div><div class="opt ">c. 3, 2, 1, 4, 6, 5</div><div class="opt correct">d. 3, 1, 4, 2, 6, 5 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.5. Sắp thứ tự của test case theo logic: bắt đầu Open/login và kết thúc là exit, tiếp theo là Search - select - edit - confirm</div><h2>Cau hoi 30</h2><div class="qtext">Which list of levels of tester independence is in the correct order, starting with the most independent first?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Tests designed by the author; tests designed by another member of the development team; tests designed by someone from a different company [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by the author; tests designed by someone from a different company.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Tests designed by someone from a different company; tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by another member of the development team. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Tests designed by someone from a different department within the company; tests designed by someone from a different company; tests designed by the author.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.5. Danh sách các cấp độ độc lập của người thử nghiệm được sắp xếp theo đúng thứ tự, bắt đầu từ mức độ độc lập cao nhất trước tiên? chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 31</h2><div class="qtext">The difference between re-testing and regression testing is:</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Re-testing is running a test again; regression testing looks for unexpected side effects [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Re-testing looks for unexpected side effects; regression testing is repeating those tests</div><div class="opt ">c. Re-testing is done after faults are fixed; regression testing is done earlier</div><div class="opt ">d. Re-testing uses different environments, regression testing uses the same environment</div><div class="opt ">e. Re-testing is done by developers, regression testing is done by independent testers</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2.3</div><h2>Cau hoi 32</h2><div class="qtext">According to the ISTQB Glossary, regression testing is required for what purpose?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To verify the success of corrective actions. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. To prevent a task from being incorrectly considered completed</div><div class="opt correct">c. To ensure that defects have not been introduced by a modification [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. To motivate better unit testing by the programmers.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2.3 mục đích của regression test? Chọn C vì có "introduced"</div><h2>Cau hoi 33</h2><div class="qtext">Maintenance testing is:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. updating tests when the software has changed [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. testing a released system that has been changed [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. testing by users to ensure that the system meets a business need</div><div class="opt ">d. testing to maintain business advantage</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 chọn D nó đang hỏi định nghĩa của Maintenance test là .... nên chỉ chọn B</div><h2>Cau hoi 34</h2><div class="qtext">Hand over of Testware is a part of which Phase:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test Analysis and Design [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test Planning and control</div><div class="opt correct">c. Test Closure Activities [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Evaluating exit criteria and reporting</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.1 "Hand over of Testware" của phase nào? xem sách chọn C</div><h2>Cau hoi 35</h2><div class="qtext">For which of the following would maintenance testing be used?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Correction of defects during the development phase [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Planned enhancements to an existing operational system. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Complaints about system quality during user acceptance testing.</div><div class="opt ">d. Integrating functions during the development of a new system.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.3 Thử nghiệm bảo trì sẽ được sử dụng cho mục đích nào sau đây? chọn B vì "enhancements" là đúng, loại A vì sửa lỗi trong giai đoạn phát triển "development phase" ko phải của maintenance test, loại C vì "Complaints" phàn nàn của KH, D loại vì "development of a new system" là phát triển hệ thống mới</div><h2>Cau hoi 36</h2><div class="qtext">Reporting Discrepancies as incidents is a part of which phase:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test Analysis and Design [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test Implementation and execution [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Test Closure Activities</div><div class="opt ">d. Evaluating exit criteria and reporting</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.1 Báo cáo sự khác biệt do sự cố là một phần của giai đoạn nào: "Discrepancies" xem sách thì là của execution test</div><h2>Cau hoi 37</h2><div class="qtext">What should be the MAIN objective during development testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. To cause as many failures as possible so that defects in the software are identified and can be fixed [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. To confirm that the system works as expected and that requirements have been met</div><div class="opt ">c. To assess the quality of the software with no intention of fixing defects</div><div class="opt ">d. To give information to stakeholders of the risk of releasing the system at a given time</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.1.1 Mục tiêu CHÍNH trong quá trình thử nghiệm phát triển là gì? chọn A tìm đc nhiều lỗi nhất có thể, B thì là mục tiêu của Acceptance test, C đánh giá chất lượng ko nằm trong mục tiêu của test, D là cung cấp thông tin cho các bên ở thời điểm Release ko phải Development test nên ko chọn D</div><h2>Cau hoi 38</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is not a part of the Test Implementation and Execution Phase?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Creating test suites from the test cases [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Executing test cases either manually or by using test execution tools</div><div class="opt ">c. Comparing actual results</div><div class="opt correct">d. Designing the Tests [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.4.1 Cái nào ko đúng thuộc giai đoạn Test Implementation and Execution? chọn D đúng, vì A của implementation, B C là của execution</div><h2>Cau hoi 39</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST describes one of the seven key principles of software testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Automated tests are better than manual tests for avoiding the Exhaustive Testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Exhaustive testing is, with sufficient effort and tool support, feasible for all software</div><div class="opt correct">c. It is normally impossible to test all input / output combinations for a software system. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. The purpose of testing is to demonstrate the absence of defects.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 1.3 Câu nào sau đây mô tả TỐT NHẤT một trong bảy nguyên tắc chính của kiểm thử phần mềm? chọn C đúng nhất, Loại A vì so sánh này ko có căn cứ, Loại B vì "Exhaustive testing" test tất cả không thể xảy ra cho tất cả phần mềm, Loại D vì "demonstrate the absence of defects" là sai vì Test ko thể chứng minh sự vắng mặt của lỗi</div></body></html>